Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:48:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] delegate_task: add fork mode for cache-prefix parity on
 the single-slot backend

tasks[] items accept "fork": true (default from delegation.fork_default).
A fork child inherits the parent's cached system prompt + ephemeral prompt,
tools[] (same order, nothing stripped) and transcript prefix verbatim, so its
first request is the parent's last request extended at the END and reuses the
warm KV prefix. Restrictions move to call time (fork_child_block_message in
the executor chokepoint); delegate_task at depth == max refuses with a
do-it-yourself error. Preflight compaction is deferred until the first
provider response so request #1 is a warm cache read. Non-fork path
unchanged. Tests: tests/tools/test_delegate_fork.py (12 tests).
